IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026":
-- PART 10A, TRANSFER OF REGISTRATION: s 363 (duty of the company to register pre-existing charges), lines 23477 to 23544 of CoA1967.txt.
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is the text's yes; JUST FALSE is the text's no in its own words; NOTHING is "the text does not say"
-- (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sge)"). A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- Division 8 of Part 4 (ss 131 and following: registration of charges) and the "default penalty" and "officer who is in default" of s 408 belong to
-- later waves; what they decide is an input here, named for the fact. Money is in Singapore dollars.

DECLARE `s 363 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 363(1) lodge with the Registrar a statement containing the prescribed particulars of the charge`

§ `Section 363(1): the statement of a pre-existing charge`

-- "If, before the registration of a foreign corporate entity, there are any charges, whether created by the foreign corporate entity or otherwise,
-- which would have been required to be registered under Division 8 of Part 4 if the foreign corporate entity had been incorporated as a company
-- under this Act, there must be lodged with the Registrar in the prescribed manner for registration, within 30 days after the date of
-- registration of the company, a statement containing the prescribed particulars of the charge."
-- First, whether the duty arises (a failed "if" is read as the text's no, reading (a) of the rule of 2026-10-29: marginal reading for a lawyer).
-- src:23479 | 363.—(1) If, before the registration of a foreign corporate entity,
-- src:23480 | there are any charges, whether created by the foreign corporate entity
-- src:23481 | or otherwise, which would have been required to be registered under
-- src:23482 | Division 8 of Part 4 if the foreign corporate entity had been
-- src:23483 | incorporated as a company under this Act, there must be lodged with
-- src:23484 | the Registrar in the prescribed manner for registration, within 30 days
-- src:23485 | after the date of registration of the company, a statement containing
-- src:23486 | the prescribed particulars of the charge.
@ref s 363(1) (src:23479-23486)
GIVEN `the charge existed before the registration of the foreign corporate entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge would have been required to be registered under Division 8 of Part 4 if the foreign corporate entity had been incorporated as a company under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 363(1) a statement of the charge must be lodged with the Registrar` MEANS
    IF `the charge existed before the registration of the foreign corporate entity` AND `the charge would have been required to be registered under Division 8 of Part 4 if the foreign corporate entity had been incorporated as a company under this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, before the registration of a foreign corporate entity, there are any charges ... which would have been required to be registered under Division 8 of Part 4 ..., there must be lodged ... a statement" (a failed "if" read as the text's no, reading (a): marginal reading for a lawyer; fork line F-363-1 in NOTES.md)

-- The last day: 30 days after the date of registration of the company.
-- src:23479 | 363.—(1) If, before the registration of a foreign corporate entity,
-- src:23480 | there are any charges, whether created by the foreign corporate entity
-- src:23481 | or otherwise, which would have been required to be registered under
-- src:23482 | Division 8 of Part 4 if the foreign corporate entity had been
-- src:23483 | incorporated as a company under this Act, there must be lodged with
-- src:23484 | the Registrar in the prescribed manner for registration, within 30 days
-- src:23485 | after the date of registration of the company, a statement containing
-- src:23486 | the prescribed particulars of the charge.
@ref s 363(1) (src:23479-23486)
GIVEN `the date of registration of the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 363(1) the last day for lodging the statement of the charge` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the date of registration of the company` 30 Days

-- Whether the statement has been lodged as the subsection requires: in the prescribed manner, with the prescribed particulars, within the 30 days.
-- JUST FALSE where the statement is lodged late or wrongly, or none is lodged and the 30 days have run out; NOTHING while the 30 days still run
-- and none is lodged (the duty is neither met nor missed). Assumes the duty arises (s 363(1) a statement of the charge must be lodged).
-- src:23479 | 363.—(1) If, before the registration of a foreign corporate entity,
-- src:23480 | there are any charges, whether created by the foreign corporate entity
-- src:23481 | or otherwise, which would have been required to be registered under
-- src:23482 | Division 8 of Part 4 if the foreign corporate entity had been
-- src:23483 | incorporated as a company under this Act, there must be lodged with
-- src:23484 | the Registrar in the prescribed manner for registration, within 30 days
-- src:23485 | after the date of registration of the company, a statement containing
-- src:23486 | the prescribed particulars of the charge.
@ref s 363(1) (src:23479-23486)
GIVEN `the date of registration of the company` IS A DATE
      `a statement of the charge has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement was lodged in the prescribed manner and contains the prescribed particulars of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the statement was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 363(1) the statement of the charge has been lodged as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `a statement of the charge has been lodged with the Registrar`
    THEN (IF `the statement was lodged in the prescribed manner and contains the prescribed particulars of the charge` AND `period: the date is within a period after` `the date of registration of the company` `the date the statement was lodged` 30 Days
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "there must be lodged with the Registrar in the prescribed manner for registration, within 30 days after the date of registration of the company, a statement containing the prescribed particulars of the charge" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (a))
    ELSE (IF `the date on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `s 363(1) the last day for lodging the statement of the charge` `the date of registration of the company`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 30 days after the date of registration of the company": the 30 days have run out and no statement has been lodged
          ELSE NOTHING)     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the 30 days have not yet run out, so the duty is neither met nor missed

-- The duty as a regulative rule: 30 days from the date of registration (AT 0). The text names no actor in subsection (1) ("there must be
-- lodged"); its heading names the company and subsection (4) its default, so the company is the party (fork line F-363-2 in NOTES.md).
-- src:23479 | 363.—(1) If, before the registration of a foreign corporate entity,
-- src:23480 | there are any charges, whether created by the foreign corporate entity
-- src:23481 | or otherwise, which would have been required to be registered under
-- src:23482 | Division 8 of Part 4 if the foreign corporate entity had been
-- src:23483 | incorporated as a company under this Act, there must be lodged with
-- src:23484 | the Registrar in the prescribed manner for registration, within 30 days
-- src:23485 | after the date of registration of the company, a statement containing
-- src:23486 | the prescribed particulars of the charge.
@ref s 363(1) (src:23479-23486)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 363 act`
`s 363(1) the company must lodge a statement of a pre-existing charge within 30 days after the date of registration` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 363(1) lodge with the Registrar a statement containing the prescribed particulars of the charge`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "no statement containing the prescribed particulars of the charge was lodged with the Registrar within 30 days after the date of registration (default under section 363(4): an offence)"

§ `Section 363(2): who may lodge`

-- "Documents and particulars required to be lodged for registration under subsection (1) may be lodged by the company concerned or by any
-- person interested in the documents."
-- src:23490 | (2) Documents and particulars required to be lodged for registration
-- src:23491 | under subsection (1) may be lodged by the company concerned or by
-- src:23492 | any person interested in the documents.
@ref s 363(2) (src:23490-23492)
GIVEN `the person is the company concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is interested in the documents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 363(2) the person may lodge the documents and particulars required to be lodged` MEANS
    IF `the person is the company concerned` OR `the person is interested in the documents`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("may be lodged by the company concerned or by any person interested in the documents") to two kinds of person; for anyone else it grants nothing and says nothing (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line F-363-3 in NOTES.md)

§ `Section 363(3): recovering the fees from the company`

-- "Where registration under subsection (1) is effected by some person other than the company concerned, that person is entitled to recover from
-- the company the amount of any fees properly paid by the person for the registration."
-- An "entitled" function with a "Where" gate: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (b), gives JUST FALSE when it fails; the grant ruling lists it
-- for a lawyer (NOTES.md, fork register F-363-4).
-- src:23496 | (3) Where registration under subsection (1) is effected by some
-- src:23497 | person other than the company concerned, that person is entitled to
-- src:23498 | recover from the company the amount of any fees properly paid by
-- src:23499 | the person for the registration.
@ref s 363(3) (src:23496-23499)
GIVEN `the registration was effected by a person other than the company concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 363(3) the person is entitled to recover the fees from the company` MEANS
    IF `the registration was effected by a person other than the company concerned`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where registration under subsection (1) is effected by some person other than the company concerned, that person is entitled to recover": a "Where" gate (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (b)), on an "entitled" function (listed for a lawyer)

-- src:23496 | (3) Where registration under subsection (1) is effected by some
-- src:23497 | person other than the company concerned, that person is entitled to
-- src:23498 | recover from the company the amount of any fees properly paid by
-- src:23499 | the person for the registration.
@ref s 363(3) (src:23496-23499)
GIVEN `the registration was effected by a person other than the company concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the fees the person properly paid for the registration, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 363(3) the amount of fees the person is entitled to recover from the company` MEANS
    IF `the registration was effected by a person other than the company concerned`
    THEN JUST `the amount of the fees the person properly paid for the registration, in Singapore dollars`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the amount is stated only "Where registration under subsection (1) is effected by some person other than the company concerned"

§ `Section 363(4): default and the offence`

DECLARE `s 363(4) penalty` HAS
    `the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `a default penalty also applies` IS A BOOLEAN

-- "If default is made in complying with subsection (1), the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall each be guilty of an
-- offence". "an officer who is in default" is s 408(3)'s phrase (a later wave): a plain input.
-- An unmet element answers JUST FALSE here (the provision's own question; split site (i), fork line F-363-5 in NOTES.md).
-- src:23503 | (4) If default is made in complying with subsection (1), the
-- src:23504 | company and every officer of the company who is in default shall
@ref s 363(4) (src:23503-23504)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 363(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) defines that phrase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 363(4) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 363(1)` AND (`the person is the company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) defines that phrase`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (1), the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall each be guilty of an offence" (an element unmet: this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts; it does not say the person is innocent of any other offence)

-- "... and shall each be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty." The amount of the default penalty is
-- s 408(1)'s (a later wave) and is not stated here.
-- src:23503 | (4) If default is made in complying with subsection (1), the
-- src:23504 | company and every officer of the company who is in default shall
-- src:23505 | each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a
-- src:23506 | fine not exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 363(4) (src:23503-23506)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 363(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) defines that phrase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 363(4) penalty`
`s 363(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 363(4) the person is guilty of an offence` `default is made in complying with section 363(1)` `the person is the company` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) defines that phrase` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 363(4) penalty` OF 1000, TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

§ `Section 363(5): a failure does not affect the charge`

-- "To avoid doubt, a failure to comply with subsection (1) does not affect the continuity of status, operation or effect of any security, right,
-- priority or obligation of the charge."
DECLARE `s 363(5) what of the charge` IS ONE OF
    `s 363(5) a security of the charge`
    `s 363(5) a right of the charge`
    `s 363(5) a priority of the charge`
    `s 363(5) an obligation of the charge`

-- src:23510 | (5) To avoid doubt, a failure to comply with subsection (1) does not
-- src:23511 | affect the continuity of status, operation or effect of any security,
-- src:23512 | right, priority or obligation of the charge.
@ref s 363(5) (src:23510-23512)
GIVEN `there has been a failure to comply with section 363(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing of the charge` IS A `s 363(5) what of the charge`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 363(5) the failure to comply with section 363(1) affects the continuity of status, operation or effect of the thing of the charge` MEANS
    IF `there has been a failure to comply with section 363(1)`
    THEN (CONSIDER `the thing of the charge`
          WHEN `s 363(5) a security of the charge` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a failure to comply with subsection (1) does not affect the continuity of status, operation or effect of any security ... of the charge"
          WHEN `s 363(5) a right of the charge` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not affect the continuity of status, operation or effect of any ... right ... of the charge"
          WHEN `s 363(5) a priority of the charge` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not affect the continuity of status, operation or effect of any ... priority ... of the charge"
          WHEN `s 363(5) an obligation of the charge` THEN JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not affect the continuity of status, operation or effect of any ... obligation of the charge"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of "a failure to comply with subsection (1)"; where there is none it says nothing

§ `Section 363(6): the Court's relief`

-- "The Court, on being satisfied — (a) that the omission to register a charge requiring registration under subsection (1), or that the omission
-- or mis-statement of any particular with respect to such charge, was accidental or due to inadvertence or to some other sufficient cause or is
-- not of a nature to prejudice the position of creditors or shareholders; or (b) that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief,
-- may on the application of the company or any person interested ... order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission
-- or mis-statement be rectified."
-- The Court's satisfaction is the Court's judgment: each ground is a conditional input. "on being satisfied" and "on the application of" are
-- "upon" gates on a "may": JUST FALSE when either fails (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (b) and (c); NOTES.md, Split sites (sge), fork line F-363-7).
-- src:23516 | (6) The Court, on being satisfied —
-- src:23518 | (a) that the omission to register a charge requiring registration
-- src:23519 | under subsection (1), or that the omission or mis‑statement
-- src:23520 | of any particular with respect to such charge, was
-- src:23521 | accidental or due to inadvertence or to some other
-- src:23526 | sufficient cause or is not of a nature to prejudice the
-- src:23527 | position of creditors or shareholders; or
-- src:23529 | (b) that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief,
-- src:23531 | may on the application of the company or any person interested and
-- src:23532 | on such terms and conditions as seem to the Court just and expedient
-- src:23533 | (including a term or condition that the rectification is to be without
-- src:23534 | prejudice to any liability already incurred by the company or any of
-- src:23535 | its officers in respect of the default) order that the time for registration
-- src:23536 | be extended or that the omission or mis‑statement be rectified.
@ref s 363(6) (src:23516-23536)
GIVEN `the Court is satisfied that the omission or mis-statement was accidental or due to inadvertence or to some other sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the omission or mis-statement is not of a nature to prejudice the position of creditors or shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application to the Court is made by the company concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application to the Court is made by a person interested` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 363(6) the Court may order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission or mis-statement be rectified` MEANS
    IF (NOT (   `the Court is satisfied that the omission or mis-statement was accidental or due to inadvertence or to some other sufficient cause`
             OR `the Court is satisfied that the omission or mis-statement is not of a nature to prejudice the position of creditors or shareholders`
             OR `the Court is satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief`))
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Court, on being satisfied — (a) ...; or (b) ..., may ... order" (an "on being satisfied" gate, read as "upon": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (b) and (c); listed in NOTES.md, Split sites (sge), fork line F-363-7, and for a lawyer)
    ELSE (IF `the application to the Court is made by the company concerned` OR `the application to the Court is made by a person interested`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may on the application of the company or any person interested" (an "on application" gate, read as "upon": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (b) and (c))

-- "... on such terms and conditions as seem to the Court just and expedient (including a term or condition that the rectification is to be without
-- prejudice to any liability already incurred by the company or any of its officers in respect of the default)".
-- src:23531 | may on the application of the company or any person interested and
-- src:23532 | on such terms and conditions as seem to the Court just and expedient
-- src:23533 | (including a term or condition that the rectification is to be without
-- src:23534 | prejudice to any liability already incurred by the company or any of
-- src:23535 | its officers in respect of the default) order that the time for registration
-- src:23536 | be extended or that the omission or mis‑statement be rectified.
@ref s 363(6) (src:23531-23536)
GIVEN `the term or condition seems to the Court just and expedient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term or condition is that the rectification is to be without prejudice to any liability already incurred by the company or any of its officers in respect of the default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 363(6) the Court may impose the term or condition on its order` MEANS
    IF `the term or condition is that the rectification is to be without prejudice to any liability already incurred by the company or any of its officers in respect of the default` OR `the term or condition seems to the Court just and expedient`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("on such terms and conditions as seem to the Court just and expedient (including ...)") whose limit is the Court's own view of what is just and expedient; a term outside it is not granted, and the text says nothing more (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line F-363-6 in NOTES.md)

§ `Section 363(7): sections 134, 135, 136 and 138 apply`

-- "In respect of any charge that is required to be lodged under subsection (1), sections 134, 135, 136 and 138 apply as if the charge were a
-- charge to which Division 8 of Part 4 applied." The four sections are a later wave's: this says only that they apply.
DECLARE `s 363(7) section` IS ONE OF
    `s 363(7) section 134`
    `s 363(7) section 135`
    `s 363(7) section 136`
    `s 363(7) section 138`
    `s 363(7) another section`

-- src:23540 | (7) In respect of any charge that is required to be lodged under
-- src:23541 | subsection (1), sections 134, 135, 136 and 138 apply as if the charge
-- src:23542 | were a charge to which Division 8 of Part 4 applied.
@ref s 363(7) (src:23540-23542)
GIVEN `the charge is required to be lodged under section 363(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the section of the Act` IS A `s 363(7) section`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 363(7) the section applies to the charge as if it were a charge to which Division 8 of Part 4 applied` MEANS
    IF `the charge is required to be lodged under section 363(1)`
    THEN (CONSIDER `the section of the Act`
          WHEN `s 363(7) another section` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "sections 134, 135, 136 and 138 apply as if ..." names four sections without "only", and says nothing of any other
          OTHERWISE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In respect of any charge that is required to be lodged under subsection (1)": for any other charge the subsection says nothing
